{
  "text": "साहित्यमा भाषाको महत्व अत्यधिक छ। यसले मानिसहरूको भावना र विचारलाई प्रकट गर्छ।",
  "source_lang": "nepali",
  "target_lang": "english"
}

{
  "text": "සාහිත්‍යය යනු මානව සභ්‍යතාවේ දර්පණයකි. එය අපගේ සංස්කෘතිය සහ සම්ප්‍රदායන් පිළිබිඹු කරයි.",
  "source_lang": "sinhala",
  "target_lang": "english"
}

{
  "text": "Literature is the mirror of human civilization. It reflects our culture, traditions, emotions, and thoughts. Through literature, we can understand the social, political, and economic conditions of different eras. Great literary works transcend time and continue to inspire generations. They provide insights into human nature and help us understand ourselves better. Literature also serves as a bridge between different cultures and languages, promoting understanding and empathy among people from diverse backgrounds.",
  "max_length": 100
}

{
  "text": "मेरो देश नेपाल\nहिमालको काखमा बसेको\nसुन्दर र शान्त देश\nयहाँका मानिसहरू मिलनसार\nसंस्कृति र परम्परा धनी",
  "source_lang": "nepali",
  "target_lang": "english"
}

{
  "text": "The rich literary traditions of Nepal and Sri Lanka span centuries, encompassing diverse forms of expression from ancient religious texts to contemporary novels and poetry. Nepali literature, written primarily in the Devanagari script, has been deeply influenced by Sanskrit traditions while also incorporating local folklore and cultural elements. The works of great Nepali poets like Laxmi Prasad Devkota and Bhanubhakta Acharya have shaped the literary landscape significantly. Similarly, Sinhala literature boasts a heritage that dates back over two millennia, with early works being primarily Buddhist religious texts written on palm leaves. The influence of Buddhism is evident throughout Sinhala literary history, from the ancient Mahavamsa chronicle to modern literary works. Both traditions have evolved to address contemporary themes while maintaining their cultural roots, making them invaluable repositories of South Asian literary heritage.",
  "max_length": 150
}
